module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.repaired_authority_lands_beside_the_unconverted_call_site

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data repaired_authority_lands_beside_the_unconverted_call_site: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "repaired_authority_lands_beside_the_unconverted_call_site" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "repaired authority lands beside the unconverted call site (INVALID STATE: a defect is diagnosed correctly, a new authority is written that fixes it, fixtures are enrolled against that authority and pass -- and the production path still calls the superseded local copy, which is left in place. The repair is complete everywhere except the one place the defect lives.)",

    "HARM IS THAT EVERY AVAILABLE SIGNAL READS GREEN. The new authority's fixtures pass because the authority is correct. The consumer's own fixtures pass because they exercise the consumer's other properties. A reviewer reading the diff sees a diagnosed defect, a principled fix and executed evidence, in that order, and the one fact that would contradict the reading -- that no edge connects them -- is the absence of a line rather than the presence of a wrong one. This is the specification-without-execution trap of DESIGN section 5 turned inside out: the code executes, the fixtures execute, and what fails to execute is the RELATIONSHIP between them.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN, gunbc#10874 2026-09-12, found by operator source review and confirmed by execution. A wheel resolver selected a package-index link with `string_contains(href, filename)` under an annotation claiming an exact match, and extracted candidates by splitting the document on double quotes and keeping every piece beginning with `https://`. The repair was correct and thorough: `extdeps.python.simple_repository_api` was written to the simple-repository spec -- comments stripped before the scan, anchor hrefs only, relative links resolved against the index, filename compared exactly on the decoded final path segment -- with fourteen fixtures, all executed, all green. The exact-filename comparison was wired into the resolver. THE EXTRACTION WAS NOT. `gunbc.spark.flashinfer_wheel_fetch` `read_index_hrefs` went on calling its own `extract_href_urls`, with the refuted `a looser extraction cannot widen selection` reasoning still standing directly above it. Fourteen green fixtures over an authority the product did not call.",

    "THE DISCRIMINATOR IS THE SPAN AND NOT THE PIECES, and it is what this row exists to make routine. No fixture on either side of a seam can see that the seam is missing: the authority's fixtures prove the authority, the consumer's fixtures prove the consumer, and both are true while the composition is wrong. The evidence that closes it runs the whole span the defect lived in -- here, from the index DOCUMENT a consumer would receive through to the RESOLUTION its fold acts on, which is the product path minus only the network call. Executed against the pre-repair revision that span answers `WheelResolved` with a locator lifted out of an HTML comment; executed against the repair it answers `WheelNotInIndex`. THE SAME RUN FALSIFIED THE OLD ALGORITHM DIRECTLY, which is the cheap form of the same check and is worth doing when a span fixture is awkward: a scratch reproduction of the superseded function, asserted to produce the WRONG answer, executed once, then deleted. Both were run on 2026-09-12 and both discriminated.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS AGAINST THREE NEIGHBOURS. It is not [[the_replaced_route_is_the_replacement_s_miss_path]]: there the old route is reachable BY DESIGN from the new one's miss arm, and every execution honestly receipts it; here there is no arm and no receipt, the new authority is simply never reached. It is not the ordinary DESIGN section 3c dangling declaration: a dangling declaration has no consumer at all and is visible as such, whereas this one HAS a consumer -- the fixtures -- which is precisely what makes it read as consumed. It is not a stale-comment class: the refuted reasoning surviving above the unconverted call site is a SYMPTOM here rather than the defect, and deleting the comment would have left the defect exactly where it was.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, usable on any repair diff and requiring no suspicion: for every authority a change ADDS, name the production call site that now reaches it, and check that the diff DELETES the thing it supersedes. A repair that adds an authority without deleting its predecessor has not finished, and the surviving predecessor is the evidence -- DESIGN section 3's single-authority law read at the granularity of one change. The author-side form is one question asked at the moment the new fixtures go green: WHICH LINE OF THE PRODUCT DID I CHANGE? If the answer is none, nothing has been repaired yet.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable. The defect was found by a person reading the product path after the repair had been reviewed and pushed, and every mechanism enrolled at the time reported success.",

    "CEILING: 2, mechanically preventable, and no higher on the evidence available. Whether a declaration is reached from an entry point's closure is decidable from the namespace tree the compiler already walks, so a change that adds a `pub` declaration reached by fixtures alone is a computable set. What is NOT decidable is whether the surviving predecessor was SUPPOSED to be superseded -- two functions computing related things is an ordinary and legitimate state -- so the mechanism can report `this change's new authority is reached only from test modules` and cannot prove that the old one should have died. That residue is a reviewer's judgment and is stated here rather than claimed away.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: a consumption census over a change's added declarations that partitions each into reached-from-a-production-entry-closure, reached-only-from-test-modules, and reached-by-nothing, sufficient for a change whose new authority is reached only by fixtures to REFUSE rather than to warn. A grep for the old function's name does not fire this trigger, and neither does a review checklist item; the population must be computed from the closure rather than searched for by spelling.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
